@startuml
title TENANT-16 — Workspace Admin Suspend or Reactivate Tenant
skinparam dpi 300
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #64748B
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #CBD5E1
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam ActorBorderColor #3B82F6
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #94A3B8
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
hide footbox
autonumber
actor "Workspace Admin" as Admin
boundary "Master Admin Dashboard" as UI
control "Spring Security" as Security
boundary "MasterTenantController" as Controller
control "MasterTenantService" as Service
database "Master PostgreSQL" as MasterDB
control "DynamicMultiTenantConnectionProvider" as Pools
collections "Local Hikari Pool Cache" as Cache

note over Admin,Security
  Requires WORKSPACE_ADMIN. Requested status must be ACTIVE or SUSPENDED.
  FAILED and PROVISIONING tenants must use retry instead.
end note
Admin -> UI: Choose Suspend or Reactivate
activate UI
UI -> Security: PATCH /master/tenants/{id}/status?status=...
activate Security
alt Unauthenticated or unauthorized
 Security --> UI: 401 Unauthorized / 403 Forbidden
 deactivate Security
 UI --> Admin: Show access error
 deactivate UI
else Authorized
 Security -> Controller: Forward request
 deactivate Security
 activate Controller
 Controller -> Service: updateTenantStatus(id, status)
 activate Service
 alt Status is not ACTIVE or SUSPENDED
  Service --> Controller: INVALID_STATUS
  deactivate Service
  Controller --> UI: 400 Bad Request
  deactivate Controller
  UI --> Admin: Show invalid status
  deactivate UI
 else Allowed target status
  Service -> MasterDB: Conditional update where current state is ACTIVE/SUSPENDED
  activate MasterDB
  MasterDB --> Service: Updated row count
  deactivate MasterDB
  alt No row updated
   Service --> Controller: INVALID_TENANT_STATE
   deactivate Service
   Controller --> UI: 409 Conflict
   deactivate Controller
   UI --> Admin: Keep current display and show conflict
   deactivate UI
  else One row updated
   Service -> MasterDB: Reload tenant by ID
   activate MasterDB
   MasterDB --> Service: Updated tenant metadata
   deactivate MasterDB
   Service -> Pools: evict(tenant.code)
   activate Pools
   Pools -> Cache: Remove and close local pool if present
   activate Cache
   Cache --> Pools: Eviction completed
   deactivate Cache
   Pools --> Service: Done
   deactivate Pools
   Service --> Controller: Updated TenantInfo
   deactivate Service
   Controller --> UI: 200 OK with safe TenantResponse
   deactivate Controller
   UI --> Admin: Refresh status display
   deactivate UI
  end
 end
end
note over MasterDB,Cache
  The database state is authoritative. Pool eviction is local to this backend process.
  A transaction started before suspension may finish; new acquisitions recheck status.
end note
@enduml
